.TH MU2EDAQ-HEARTBEATMONITOR-API 7 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-heartbeatmonitor t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor\-api \- heartbeat wire format and HTTP API
.SH DESCRIPTION
.SS Heartbeat datagram
A heartbeat is one UDP datagram, sent to port 9999 over IPv4 or IPv6
(unicast, broadcast or multicast), containing one UTF\-8 JSON object:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
{"name": "daq\-node\-01",
 "timestamp": "2026\-10\-06T19:21:24.594+00:00",
 "status": "OK"}
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B name
Required string; whitespace\-trimmed; the sender's identity.
A new name creates a new entry.
.TP
.B timestamp
Optional, conventionally an ISO\-8601 UTC string from the sender.
Displayed only.
Liveness is computed from the time the monitor received the datagram, so the
sender's clock does not matter.
.TP
.B status
Optional, conventionally a short string.
Displayed only; it does not affect the healthy or timed\-out state.
.PP
There is no version field, no acknowledgement and no authentication.
Unknown keys are ignored.
.PP
Non\-JSON or non\-UTF\-8 datagrams, and objects without a non\-empty
.BR name ,
are logged and dropped.
Valid JSON that is not an object, or an object whose
.B name
is not a string, currently terminates the receiving listener thread; senders
must never emit such datagrams.
.SS Sender encodings
.BR heartbeat_sender.py (1)
uses Python
.B json.dumps
defaults: spaces after
.B ,
and
.BR : ,
non\-ASCII escaped as
.BR \euXXXX ,
microsecond timestamps (the fraction is omitted when it is exactly zero).
.BR heartbeat_sender (1)
and
.BR libheartbeat_sender_lib (3)
emit compact JSON, raw UTF\-8, and millisecond timestamps.
Both decode to the same object.
.SS HTTP API
Served on port 8081 in the control room; no authentication.
.TP
.B GET /api/systems
JSON object with
.B systems
(list sorted by name; each entry has
.BR name ,
.BR age_seconds ,
.BR age_display ,
.BR sent_timestamp ,
.BR status ,
.BR source ,
.BR description ,
.BR timeout ,
.BR timed_out ,
.BR state ),
.BR total ,
.BR healthy ,
.B unhealthy
and
.BR server_time .
.B state
is
.B error
if the age exceeds the timeout, else
.BR ok .
.TP
.B GET /api/health
.B {\(dqstatus\(dq: \(dqok\(dq|\(dqdegraded\(dq, \(dqtotal\(dq: N, \(dqhealthy\(dq: M}
with HTTP 200 in both cases.
It covers only senders currently known; a sender removed after
.B cleanup_after
seconds of silence, or never heard from, is not counted.
.TP
.B GET /stream
Server\-Sent Events; one
.B data:
line carrying the
.B /api/systems
object every
.B refresh_interval
seconds, for as long as the client stays connected.
.TP
.B GET /api/theme
.B {\(dqtheme\(dq: \(dqdark\(dq|\(dqlight\(dq}
.TP
.B POST /api/theme
Body
.BR {\(dqtheme\(dq: \(dqlight\(dq} ;
changes the default theme for all viewers.
400 on any other value.
.TP
.BR "GET /" ", " "GET /settings"
Dashboard and settings HTML.
.SS Service discovery
With
.B mu2edaq\-discovery
installed the monitor answers DISCOVER requests as
.BR app=heartbeatmonitor ,
.BR scheme=http ,
the HTTP port, and
.B meta
.BR {\(dqudp_port\(dq: \(dq9999\(dq} .
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
echo \-n '{"name":"probe","status":"OK"}' | nc \-u \-w1 127.0.0.1 9999
curl \-s localhost:8081/api/health
curl \-sN localhost:8081/stream | head \-c 400
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR heartbeat_monitor.py (1),
.BR heartbeat_sender.py (1),
.BR heartbeat_sender (1),
.BR libheartbeat_sender_lib (3),
.BR heartbeat_config.yaml (5)
